 short sword.519/519/3302/183>nHorde leaves north.You are standing in a large hallway.The walls are made out of burning fires, and if you look toolong into them you start to see scenes from battles foughtages ago between the various lords of this realm.    There are two obvious exits: north and southA horde of many wandering undeads (undead)519/519/3302/183>You miss.Hp: 499(519) Sp: 3294(3556) Ep: 182(189)You miss.Hp: 499(519) Sp: 3294(3556) Ep: 181(189)There is no corpse to bury.You pummel Horde causing just light scratches.Hp: 499(519) Sp: 3294(3556) Ep: 180(189)Horde weakly hits you leaving large wounds.Horde weakly hits you rupturing skin.Horde misses you.Horde weakly hits you opening small wounds.A wraith appears above the horde of undeads and gazes Drude!That really HURT!qYou are not casting anything.499/519/3294/180>You miss.Hp: 204(519) Sp: 3294(3556) Ep: 179(189)Horde starts concentrating on an offensive spell.You are STUNNED by the force of Horde's attack!Horde weakly hits you rupturing skin.Horde weakly hits you causing nasty scrapes.Horde weakly hits you causing nasty scrapes.Horde weakly hits you opening small wounds.Horde mumbles the magic word: 'exs'nYou are stunned and unable to move.204/519/3294/179>You are stunned are unable to fight back.You are stunned and unable to do anything.Horde weakly hits you leaving large wounds.Horde weakly hits you causing nasty scrapes.Your wounds are SEVERE!Horde weakly hits you rupturing skin.Your wounds are SEVERE!Horde weakly hits you opening small wounds.Your wounds are SEVERE!Horde looks at the ground and shouts: 'sol'nYou are stunned and unable to move.111/519/3294/179>nYou are stunned and unable to move.111/519/3294/179>nYou are stunned and unable to move.111/519/3294/179>You are stunned are unable to fight back.You are stunned and unable to do anything.Horde weakly hits you leaving large wounds.Your wounds are SEVERE!The pain eases and allows you to move again.Horde shouts: 'Drude bites the dust!'{inform}: Drude dies.So there is something really wrong there ... Okay I made the mistake ofcasting a spell after my horde had killed the monster but still that isno good reason for it to suddenly start attacking me after I'd fled away ...Things like that have happened a few times today to me .. but mostly thehorde suddenly wouldn't follow me so I could type 'stop'Maybe this could help to make the necro code bug less ...Cheers, Drude**"
